From ff9934dde576b0de1acaa90d66a60f3c6986b143 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] scratch archive: judge .git markers through the
 scan's dir fd; document gzip L1 size cost

Follow-up to PR #2175 review 5890654767 (card t_01a1d4c6f753671c), three
non-blocking nits:

1. Size note. `_GZIP_LEVEL = 1` now carries its trade-off next to the
   constant and in the module docstring: payloads are ~14% larger than at
   level 9 (real 547 MB worker tree: L9 59.8 s / 180.2 MB, L6 18.6 s /
   181.6 MB, L1 8.3 s / 205.2 MB). Reverse with `_GZIP_LEVEL = 6`; readers
   need no change. No other doc covers scratch archive size or budget
   (docs/kanban-workspace-publication.md and the kanban user guide describe
   only worktree retention), so the module is the single place.
2. `_is_gitlink` no longer re-walks the path from `/` via `_open_root` per
   `.git` marker (O(depth) opens each). `_scan` takes an `on_git_file`
   callback, called for each regular `.git` while its directory fd is
   open; `_find_repos` judges markers there through that fd, so the read is
   tied to the exact directory the scan saw. The O_NOFOLLOW open + scanned
   lstat signature match and the post-write marker signature re-check are
   unchanged. OSErrors inside the judge now surface through `_scan`'s own
   "scan uncertain" refusal (same message as before).
3. `_is_gitlink` docstring says it handles regular files only (the caller
   treats any other `.git` type as a gitlink).

Proof:
- RED (module reverted, tests kept): test_marker_judged_against_its_scanned_stat
  and new test_marker_read_through_the_scans_own_directory_fd fail
  (old signature; `_open_root` called per marker).
- GREEN: test_kanban_scratch_gc_archive + _custody + _owned_jobs (every
  test file importing the module): 203 passed, 0 failed. The race test
  test_marker_rewritten_into_gitlink_after_judgement_keeps_workspace passes.
- New test also swaps the marker's directory by path mid-scan: the fd path
  reads the scanned directory's data marker instead of the replacement's
  gitlink.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
